senses.gloss:
गाह् (cf. √ गाध्) cl. 1. Ā. गा॑हते (ep. also P. ˚हति; perf. जगाहे fut. 2nd गाहिष्यते [fut. 1st -गाहिता, or -गाढा, Kāś. on Pāṇ. vii, 2, 44]; aor. अगाहिष्ट [Bhaṭṭ. xv, 59] or अगाढ, Pāṇ. viii, 3, 13, Sch. [not in Kāś.]; inf. गाहितुम्)
to dive into, bathe in, plunge into (acc.), penetrate, enter deeply into (acc.), AitBr. iii, 48, 9; TāṇḍyaBr. xiv f.; Kauś.; MBh. &c. (with कक्षाम्, ‘to be a match for (gen.)’, Vcar. ii, 11);
to roam, range, rove, Megh. 49; Pāṇ. ii, 4, 30, Kāś.; Bhaṭṭ.;
to be absorbed in (acc.), Kum. v, 46.
